P1-1 — Prior stage-gate finding remains only partially fixed.
The contract now states that no status “at or past freeze” may pass without Ariadne, Nabu, and Vulcan PASS reviews (docs/spec/SMP1.md:509-513). The checker, however, enforces review fields only for FROZEN_STATUS and COMPLETE_STATUS (scripts/check_smp1_contract.py:230-233). It explicitly admits DRAFT_IN_PROGRESS_STATUS and IMPLEMENTED_STATUS as valid implementation statuses (lines 20-24, 217-218), and neither is review-gated. Therefore S20_400_CONTRACT_DRAFT_S20_410_IMPLEMENTED_REVIEW_PENDING can still pass the checker without the three required PASS reviews. The prior P1-8 is not closed.

P1-2 — The new below/above negotiated-version rule is unreachable on decode.
Revision 11 says a later frame below the selected version answers PROTOCOL_DOWNGRADE and one above answers PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED (docs/spec/SMP1.md:188-192). ProtocolFrame::validate rejects every protocol_version unequal to the compile-time PROTOCOL_VERSION as VERSION_UNSUPPORTED (crates/sley-protocol/src/lib.rs:996-999), and decode_frame invokes that validation before Server::dispatch (lib.rs:1185). Consequently a version-0 frame under selected version 1 is answered VERSION_UNSUPPORTED, not DOWNGRADE. Server::dispatch contains the intended SelectedProfile::check_claim branch (crates/sley-protocol/src/server.rs:532-540), but malformed-version frames cannot reach it. The added test also encodes only through the rejecting codec and expects VERSION_UNSUPPORTED for both 0 and 2, so it pins the contradiction rather than the contract rule. This is a stable wire-code/T45 mismatch.

P2: none added; investigation stopped after the P1 verdict was decisive.
